## liquid-tower

liquid-tower-ask = Where in a cylinder of four liquids does a piece of acrylic glass stop?
liquid-tower-title = Bodies and liquids of different densities in one cylinder
liquid-tower-question = Into a measuring cylinder we pour in turn 50 mL each of glycerol, water, sunflower oil and ethanol — slowly, down the wall. Then we let in a steel nut, a piece of acrylic glass, a piece of polyethylene and a pine cube. Acrylic glass sinks in water. Where will it stop in our cylinder?
liquid-tower-choices = On the bottom: it sinks in water after all
liquid-tower-choices-2 = At the boundary of glycerol and water
liquid-tower-choices-3 = At the boundary of water and oil
liquid-tower-setup = A 250 mL measuring cylinder, glycerol, water, sunflower oil, ethanol (50 mL each), food colouring, a steel nut, pieces of acrylic glass and polyethylene, a pine cube
